CORE unix
main.c
--pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion r0 == -1 && errno == EINVAL: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion r == 0: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line \d+ dereference failure: deallocated dynamic object in \*\(\(char \*\)p\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
--
^warning: ignoring
--
munmap only fails for invalid arguments, and a successful munmap releases the
mapping.
